# social_jira4 rr10dcp — score every cell of the deception study with deepseek-v4-flash-0731.
#
# NOTHING IS GENERATED HERE. The rollout jobs (rr10dcp_or_*.sub, rr10dcp_vllm_*.sub) ran with
# --no-judge, so every cell is on disk unscored. This job runs the three critics (CATEGORY,
# SOUNDNESS, AT-STAKE) over the frozen transcripts: one judge, one code path, every cell. Run dirs
# are opened read-only; only the judgments tree is written.
#
# SAFE TO RUN EARLY, AND AGAIN. Cells are discovered from disk on each pass and resume is per
# rollout, so submitting this while generation is still in flight scores what exists and a later
# submission picks up the rest. Nothing is paid for twice.
#
# ONE JOB PER DECEPTION LEVEL, via `queue LEVEL in`. The split is not for wall-clock alone — it
# bounds API pressure. Total in-flight judge calls is jobs x --workers x --critic-workers, so
# 3 x 4 x 6 = 72 here. rr24 ran 96 across four jobs without rate-limit failures, so this sits
# comfortably under the only precedent we have. A single job at the same internal concurrency would
# be a third of the throughput; fourteen one-per-cell jobs would be 252 in flight, which is how the
# 429s in the rr10 preflight sweeps were produced.
#
# THE LEVELS ARE UNEVEN, deliberately. On this filesystem `allow` and `forbid` are 6 cells each
# (4 OpenRouter + 2 vLLM) while `none` is 2 — the four OpenRouter base cells were collected before
# the axis existed and are judged from the local copy under outputs/rr10dcp/cells. The `none` job
# will therefore finish early; that is expected, not a stall.
#
# JUDGE ROUTING. order [DeepInfra] with allow_fallbacks TRUE — DeepInfra first (cheapest endpoint
# for this model), anything else if it rate-limits. Deliberately NOT a hard pin: ~13,000 judge calls
# on one upstream with fallbacks off is precisely the 429 three preflight sweeps produced during
# rr10. Every call records which upstream served it, so how often it left DeepInfra is countable
# from verdicts.jsonl rather than a matter of trust.
#
# SEAT NAME IS LOAD-BEARING. `dsflash0731` is the same seat the local base-cell pass wrote, so the
# two halves of the study merge into one judgments tree without translation.
#
# COST. ~280 rollouts x ~$0.066 measured on the base cells, scaled down by flash-0731's cheaper
# tokens: on the order of $15. cost.json is written per cell and accumulates across invocations.
#
# AFTER IT FINISHES, rebuild the study-wide table (no model calls, reads what is on disk):
#   bash experiments/social_jira4/cluster/run_sj4_rejudge.sh --cells \
#       --root experiments/social_jira4/outputs/rr10dcp/cells --seat dsflash0731 --summarize
#
# CPU-ONLY. Submit with `condor_submit_bid 25`.
executable = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/run_sj4_rejudge.sh
arguments  = "--cells --root experiments/social_jira4/outputs/rr10dcp/cells --cells-prefix $(LEVEL)_ --seat dsflash0731 --judge-model deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731 --judge-provider-routing {""order"":[""DeepInfra""],""allow_fallbacks"":true} --workers 4 --critic-workers 6"

output = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/rr10dcp_judge_$(LEVEL).out
error  = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/rr10dcp_judge_$(LEVEL).err
log    = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/rr10dcp_judge_$(LEVEL).log

request_cpus   = 4
request_memory = 8192
request_disk   = 4G

queue LEVEL in (none, allow, forbid)
